# Kodi Settings and Localization

## settings.xml Format (v1)

The settings file uses Kodi's v1 format at `resources/settings.xml`:

```xml
<settings version="1">
  <section id="plugin.video.themoviedb.helper">
    <category id="general" label="$LOCALIZE[32000]" help="">
      <group id="1" label="$LOCALIZE[32001]">
        <setting id="my_setting" type="boolean" label="$LOCALIZE[32002]" help="$LOCALIZE[32003]" default="true">
          <level>0</level>
          <control type="toggle" />
        </setting>
      </group>
    </category>
  </section>
</settings>
```

### Hierarchy

`<settings>` -> `<section>` (one per addon) -> `<category>` (tabs) -> `<group>` (visual grouping) -> `<setting>` (individual settings).

### Setting Types

| Type | Description | Control |
|---|---|---|
| `boolean` | On/off toggle | `<control type="toggle" />` |
| `string` | Text input | `<control type="edit" />` |
| `integer` | Numeric value | `<control type="edit" format="integer" />` or `<control type="spinner" />` |
| `number` | Float value | `<control type="edit" format="number" />` |
| `path` | File/folder path | `<control type="button" format="path" />` |
| `action` | Clickable action | `<control type="button" format="action" />` |
| `addon` | Addon picker | `<control type="button" format="addon" />` |

### Setting Visibility Levels

| Level | Description |
|---|---|
| 0 | Basic -- always visible |
| 1 | Standard |
| 2 | Advanced |
| 3 | Expert |
| 4 | Internal -- never shown in GUI |

### Dependencies Between Settings

Use `<dependencies>` to show/hide settings conditionally:

```xml
<setting id="child_setting" type="string" label="...">
  <dependencies>
    <dependency type="visible" setting="parent_setting" operator="is">true</dependency>
  </dependencies>
</setting>
```

## strings.po Localization

Localization files live in `resources/language/resource.language.<locale>/strings.po`.

### Format

```po
msgctxt "#32000"
msgid "General"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32001"
msgid "My New Feature"
msgstr ""
```

- `msgctxt` -- unique numeric ID prefixed with `#`.
- `msgid` -- English source text.
- `msgstr` -- translation (empty in `en_gb`, filled in other locales).

### String ID Ranges

- **0 -- 31999**: Reserved for Kodi core. Never use these.
- **32000+**: Addon-specific strings. This addon uses IDs starting at `#32000`.
- When adding new strings, find the next unused ID by checking the existing `strings.po` file.

### Referencing Strings

- In `settings.xml`: `$LOCALIZE[32000]`
- In Python: `xbmcaddon.Addon().getLocalizedString(32000)` or use the addon's `get_localized(32000)` wrapper from `tmdbhelper.lib.addon.plugin`.

### Adding New Strings

1. Add the new `msgctxt`/`msgid`/`msgstr` entry to `resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po`.
2. Use sequential IDs -- do not leave gaps unless reusing a deleted ID.
3. If adding translations, update the corresponding locale files.
4. Always add a string before referencing it in `settings.xml` or Python code.

## Existing Locales

This addon supports 16 locales: `en_gb` (default), `de_de`, `es_es`, `fr_fr`, `it_it`, `ja_jp`, `ko_kr`, `nl_nl`, `pl_pl`, `pt_br`, `pt_pt`, `ru_ru`, `sv_se`, `uk_ua`, `zh_cn`, `zh_tw`.
